sparky-stereo-browser (@DEBVERSION@) unstable; urgency=medium

  * WebGL pages without WebXR are drawn in stereo by the browser (the
    camera hack, webgl.stereo-camera.enabled, on in this package). The
    page's camera, a perspective projection or a view-projection product
    uploaded as a plain uniform or in a uniform block, is recognised when
    the page uploads it. Each draw into the page's canvas is made twice,
    once per eye, with two parallel cameras whose frustums meet at five
    times the near distance (off-axis, never toed in). 2D drawn with an
    orthographic camera stays at the screen's depth. Shadow maps and other
    passes into the page's own framebuffers are drawn once. The canvas is
    declared full side by side, left eye first.
  * Video that WebRender draws into a surface of its own (software
    WebRender, and video decoded into plain buffers, such as VP9 through
    libvpx) carries its stereo mark to that surface and is declared like
    DMABuf video. Views in another order or on top of each other are copied
    side by side, on the GPU or in memory.
  * Frames decoded in software take the stream's frame packing SEI.
  * The 3D Video menu gets Swap Eyes: each eye sees the other view, over
    the file's mark, the user's choice and the picture's shape, so a video
    marked the wrong way round is corrected by its viewer. In the edition's
    eight languages.
  * The user's choice in the 3D Video menu also applies to video in plain
    buffers.
  * The browser decides how a video holds its views through
    libstereo-policy, the edition's shared stereo policy in plain C (the
    stream's or the file's mark, the user's choice, the frame's shape, Swap
    Eyes over them, and full or half views), as Dolphin, the thumbnailers
    and the players do. It depends on libstereo-policy1 instead of
    libstereo-layer1, so no Qt library is loaded into the browser.
  * The screen is offered as a WebXR immersive device whenever an output
    shows stereo 3D, or can (a 3D mode of the display's own, the virtual
    3D modes, a pair of outputs), even beside 2D outputs; KWin shows each
    output what it can. Where no output does, the device is not offered
    and pages take their own 2D path.
  * The camera hack presents both eyes only where the compositor takes
    declared stereo content; elsewhere, X11 included, pages draw as before.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  @DATE@

sparky-stereo-browser (6.7.5-0+stereo3d3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Pages declare stereo only through WebXR: the stereolayout canvas
    attribute is gone.
  * The screen is a WebXR immersive device (dom.vr.flat.enabled): an
    "immersive-vr" session shows its canvas full screen, each eye its view,
    with a window projection at the viewer's distance; the mouse, the wheel
    and the keyboard move the view.
  * Inline sessions take the "inline-stereo" feature: the page's canvas
    holds both views side by side and is declared on its own surface.
    Inline projections keep the canvas's shape.
  * Videos say they hold two views in this order: the stream's frame
    packing SEI, the container's mark (Matroska StereoMode, every value of
    RFC 9559 Table 5, with its DisplayWidth and DisplayHeight; the MP4 st3d
    box), the user's choice in the new 3D Video menu, and last the
    picture's shape through libstereo-layer's C entry. A mark without the
    size of a view takes full size views from a picture at least 2.5 times
    as wide as high (side by side) or at most 1.2 (top and bottom).
  * Top and bottom and right eye first pictures, and videos clipped on the
    side, are copied on the GPU into two views side by side, left eye
    first, before they are declared.
  * The stereo-layer policy wrapper is gone: the browser calls
    libstereo-layer's C entry itself.
  * The 3D Video menu is translated into Polish, Brazilian Portuguese,
    French, Japanese, Korean and Chinese (simplified and traditional).

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 01:04:08 +0000

sparky-stereo-browser (6.7.5-0+stereo3d2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Pictures that hold two views, full side by side with the left eye first,
    are declared on their own Wayland surface to Stereo KWin through
    libstereo-declare: videos marked so in their file (WebM StereoMode),
    videos without a mark that the stereo-layer policy finds side by side,
    and WebGL canvases the page marks with stereolayout="stereo-left-right".
  * WebRender's native compositor is on (gfx.webrender.compositor), so that
    videos and canvases get surfaces of their own.
  * The stereo-layer policy wrapper, libstereo-policy.so, is built and
    installed beside the browser.
  * Waterfox's strings that mean this browser take the brand name; the names
    of BrowserWorks' services stay.
  * A profile folder of its own, ~/.sparky-stereo-browser.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Tue, 13 Oct 2026 03:57:57 +0000

